    {
      "id": "chatcmpl-E5336lkI3MHKJCgPNCawxwOfDLye7",
      "role": "assistant",
      "created": 1784872068,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I can’t compute this right now because the mandatory MedCP clinical database connection failed:\n\n```text\nAdaptive Server connection failed (QCDIDDWDB001.ucsfmedicalcenter.org)\n```\n\nI also checked for MedCP-provided resources, but none were returned. Without access to the COPD cohort prescription table, I can’t count active prescriptions by bronchodilator mechanism.\n\nOnce MedCP is reachable, the analysis should be:\n\n1. identify COPD cohort patients,\n2. retrieve active bronchodilator prescriptions,\n3. normalize drugs/classes,\n4. map to KG mechanisms such as:\n   - β2-adrenergic receptor agonism,\n   - muscarinic receptor antagonism,\n   - phosphodiesterase inhibition,\n   - methylxanthine/adenosine receptor-related bronchodilation,\n5. count active prescriptions or patients per mechanism,\n6. rank mechanisms by representation."
        }
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "userVisible": true,
        "agentVisible": true
      }
